Package: SIR
Title: Isotonic Bliss Synergy Testing for Drug Combinations
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Amir", "Asiaee", , "amir.asiaeetaheri@vumc.org", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("James P.", "Long", role = "aut"),
    person("Samhita", "Pal", role = "aut"),
    person("Heather H.", "Pua", role = "aut"),
    person("Kevin R.", "Coombes", role = "aut"))
Description: Tests drug-combination viability matrices relative to Bliss
    independence using isotonic single-agent and surface fits. A standardized
    excess statistic is calibrated by a plug-in parametric bootstrap at exact
    Bliss with two-stage Monte Carlo. Includes design-matched companion mean
    tests, region scans, activity summaries, missing-well and replicate handling,
    and within-family false discovery rate adjustment. Calls the bundled
    Python implementation through 'reticulate'.
